  |

error[E1001]: `xs[0].len` is used here after its value moved away
  --> mem:///main.lu:13:16
   |
 8 |             keep = move xs[i]
   |                         ----- `xs[i]` moved here
...
13 |     keep.len + xs[0].len
   |                ^^^^^^^^^ used after the move
   |
   = note: `xs[0].len` may reach the moved `xs[i]`: an index that is not a literal is one place
     with every other index of its container [mem.model.place.elem]. Distinct literal indices
     stay usable.
   = note: re-initializing the place (assigning to it) also makes it usable again.
help: to keep the original, copy it at the move
   |
 8 |             keep = move copy xs[i]
   |
